      "section": "opening",
      "slot": "opening",
      "text": "Aspose.Imaging FOSS for .NET is a free, open-source .NET library — an Aspose.Imaging alternative that does zero-dependency image format detection and header probing. ImageProbe identifies a file's format and reads its basic properties — dimensions, bit depth, and frame count — directly from the file header, so you know what a file is and how big it is, fast, without pulling in a full imaging stack to decode a single pixel. It has no NuGet dependencies and targets netstandard2.0 and net8.0.",
      "fact_ids": [
        "inherited_unit:004.paragraph"
      ]
    },
    {
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:1",
      "text": "Detects 14 image formats as a free, open source Aspose.Imaging alternative to a full decode pipeline — ImageProbe.DetectFormat() reads only the file's signature bytes and returns an ImageFormat value, so identifying a file never requires pulling in a full imaging stack.",
      "fact_ids": [
        "public_symbol:aspose.imaging.foss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:2",
      "text": "ImageProbe.Probe() reads a format's real header fields directly into an ImageInfo — width, height, bit depth, and frame count — for PNG, JPEG, GIF, BMP, WEBP (lossy, lossless, and extended), ICO, TIFF, PSD, EMF, WMF, DICOM, DJVU, AVIF, and HEIC/HEIF, as a free open source .NET image manipulation API with no decode step.",
      "fact_ids": [
        "public_symbol:aspose.imaging.foss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:3",
      "text": "The library builds from src/Aspose.Imaging.Foss/Aspose.Imaging.Foss.csproj, which declares zero PackageReference entries — every format's header parsing is implemented natively within the library.",
      "fact_ids": [
        "dependency:none",
        "package:name"
      ]
    },
    {
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:4",
      "text": "Probe() never throws on a signature match it can't fully parse — malformed or truncated input comes back as an ImageInfo with only Format set, never an exception, so a probing pipeline can run unattended over untrusted input.",
      "fact_ids": [
        "public_symbol:aspose.imaging.foss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:5",
      "text": "The library multi-targets netstandard2.0 and net8.0 to support both legacy and modern .NET runtimes.",
      "fact_ids": [
        "package:target_framework"
      ]
    },
    {
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:6",
      "text": "Both synchronous and async entry points exist for the same operation — ProbeFile()/ProbeFileAsync() and Probe()/ProbeAsync() — so a probe can run on an ASP.NET request thread without blocking it.",
      "fact_ids": [
        "public_symbol:aspose.imaging.foss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "section": "api_reference",
      "slot": "intro",
      "text": "Aspose.Imaging FOSS for .NET exposes Aspose.Imaging FOSS for .NET as its sole public namespace, targeting netstandard2.0 and net8.0. The ImageProbe class serves as the single entry point, returning an ImageFormat value and an ImageInfo record for every supported format.",
      "fact_ids": [
        "identity:repository",
        "package:name",
        "package:target_framework",
        "public_symbol:aspose.imaging.foss",
        "public_symbol:aspose.imaging.foss.imageformat",
        "public_symbol:aspose.imaging.foss.imageinfo",
        "public_symbol:aspose.imaging.foss.imageprobe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "section": "api_reference",
      "slot": "hub:public_symbol:aspose.imaging.foss",
      "text": "ImageProbe is the library's single entry point; it returns an ImageFormat value and an ImageInfo record for every supported format.",
      "fact_ids": [
        "public_symbol:aspose.imaging.foss",
        "public_symbol:aspose.imaging.foss.imageformat",
        "public_symbol:aspose.imaging.foss.imageinfo",
        "public_symbol:aspose.imaging.foss.imageprobe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "section": "scope_limitations",
      "slot": "scope",
      "text": "Aspose.Imaging FOSS for .NET provides format detection and header metadata inspection via the ImageProbe class; it reads format signatures and header fields but never decodes pixel data, so it does not support rendering, editing, or format conversion.",
      "fact_ids": [
        "identity:repository",
        "inherited_unit:030.paragraph",
        "inherited_unit:037.paragraph",
        "inherited_unit:040.paragraph",
        "inherited_unit:052.list",
        "package:name",
        "package:target_framework",
        "public_symbol:aspose.imaging.foss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "section": "scope_limitations",
      "slot": "limitation:1",
      "text": "Detection and metadata only. ImageProbe identifies a format and reads its header fields; it never decodes pixel data, so there is no rendering, editing, or format-conversion capability anywhere in the library.",
      "fact_ids": [
        "inherited_unit:052.list",
        "public_symbol:aspose.imaging.foss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "section": "scope_limitations",
      "slot": "limitation:2",
      "text": "Frame count reflects only what the container itself records. It is a real, computed count for GIF, ICO, TIFF, and bundled multi-page DJVU (DJVM); every other supported format reports a fixed 1 for a successfully parsed header, since none of their headers carry a genuine frame or page count. An indirect (multi-file) DJVM document, or a truncated bundled one, reports FrameCount as null, since its pages can't all be seen from the one file.",
      "fact_ids": [
        "inherited_unit:052.list",
        "public_symbol:aspose.imaging.foss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "section": "scope_limitations",
      "slot": "limitation:3",
      "text": "Non-placeable WMF is detected but not dimensioned. The classic (non-placeable) WMF header carries no bounding rectangle, so Probe returns a format-only ImageInfo for it; only the placeable WMF header (identified by its own magic number) yields Width/Height. Placeable-WMF dimensions assume a conventional 96 DPI target, since the header only stores units-per-inch bounds.",
      "fact_ids": [
        "inherited_unit:052.list",
        "public_symbol:aspose.imaging.foss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "section": "scope_limitations",
      "slot": "limitation:4",
      "text": "DICOM parsing stops at the first undefined-length element. A sequence or encapsulated pixel-data element with an undefined length ends the walk rather than being parsed, since Rows/Columns/BitsAllocated always precede such elements in a conformant file.",
      "fact_ids": [
        "inherited_unit:052.list",
        "public_symbol:aspose.imaging.foss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "section": "scope_limitations",
      "slot": "limitation:5",
      "text": "CDR support is planned but not yet implemented — no CdrFormatHandler exists in the current source tree.",
      "fact_ids": [
        "inherited_unit:052.list",
        "public_symbol:aspose.imaging.foss"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "omitted": []
}
